RIC. Excess kurtosis {−0.72, −0.85, −0.14} vs Gumbel +2.4 — PLATYKURTIC. KS to free Gauss = {0.061, 0.062, 0.050}; KS to FHK Gumbel(1/2) = {0.088, 0.169, 0.128}; **ratio (Gauss/Gumbel) ∈ {0.69, 0.37, 0.39}** — Gauss preferred at every T-anchor. Vuong z (Gauss vs Gumbel) = {−1.79, −1.43, −1.58} (joint Z ≈ −2.8). Selberg-resid drops {−0.004, −0.068, −0.063} systematically less negative than FHK predicts {−0.167, −0.304, −0.137}; max deviation Z = +2.225 at T = 10⁴ → 10⁶ — below 5σ A-grade threshold; data leans toward Selberg's `c = 0` over FHK's `c = −0.75` but inconclusive. Pointwise log\|ζ\| variance is Selberg-typical (within 15% of (1/2) log log T at all 3 T). Argmax distribution approximately uniform (KS 0.16-0.20). **Mechanism for closure mode I**: Saksman-Webb 2018 proved ζ on mesoscopic scale converges to GMC; FHK Gumbel-limit is a refined consequence applying log-correlation theory to GMC. The convergence rate at finite T is NOT addressed in the published literature. Empirically: mean convergence is FAST (T-stable at T = 10⁴), shape convergence is SLOW (still ~Gaussian at T = 10⁶). Pre-freezing log-correlated noise is approximately Gaussian (CLT on scale-summed log-correlation kernel); freezing transition responsible for Gumbel heavy tail has not yet activated. **First quantitative bound on FHK convergence rate at finite T** (project-internal or published). **Adds EDGE E7.18**: M_T-mean = −0.657 ± 0.045 T-INDEPENDENT but M_T-shape ~Gaussian (var 1.47× FHK, skew ≈ 0.10 vs Gumbel +1.14, ex-kurt ≈ −0.4 vs Gumbel +2.4) at T ≤ 10⁶; FHK Gumbel limit shape NOT finite-T-detectable. First ζ-amplitude edge of the project, complementary to E7.1 / E1.10 / E3.13 / E7.15 (all position-side). Empirical FHK universal intercept M_∞-mean = −0.657 → GMC moment-generating constant `c ≈ 0.151` (under FHK Gumbel form), vs RMT-side prediction `c ≈ 0.79` (Bourgade-Kuan 2014); factor-5 finite-T gap. **Cross-domain ingredient (Gaussian multiplicative chaos / FHK extreme-value statistics) performed real work**: first project quantitative use; CROSS_DOMAIN_TECHNIQUES.md §3 row "Gaussian multiplicative chaos / FHK extreme-value statistics of \|ζ(1/2 + it)\|" promoted PROPOSED (C7) → USED I with edge E7.18. **Channelled mathematician**: Bourgain (extreme-value statistics of log-correlated random fields). **Successors proposed (S133)**: C7.a mesoscopic-window FHK at the Saksman-Webb scale (window length δ = (log T)^{1/2}, same cross-domain, single session); C7.b joint argmax × prime alignment (test if argmax positions correlate with prime-power loci `(p^k log p)/(2π) mod 1` — UNUSED HL-pair-correlation extension); C7.c higher-order Keating-Snaith joint moments μ_λ at λ ∈ {2, 3, 4} (NEW cross-domain Keating-Snaith arXiv:math/0006046, reuses S133 per-window data). Cites E7.1, E1.10, E3.13, E7.15. Cross-domain refs: Fyodorov-Hiary-Keating 2012 *PRL* 108 = arXiv:1202.4713; Saksman-Webb 2018 = arXiv:1609.00027; Arguin-Belius-Bourgade 2017 *CMP* 349 = arXiv:1612.08575; Bourgade-Kuan 2014 *CPAM* 67; Selberg 1946 (Selberg CLT for log\|ζ\|). See experiments/analytic/zeta_structure/fhk_amplitude_max/. | 133 |
