(x)=1/((1+x)log2) at cosine ≥0.9919 for h ∈ {χ_P, λ, Λ}; arithmetic content lives in eigenvalue, not eigenfunction. Rayleigh-quotient closed form λ_0^h ≈ Σ_n h(n)·a_n with a_n=T_n/||g||², T_n=∫₀¹dx/[(1+x)(x+n)(x+n+1)·log²2] explicit (partial fractions); for n≥2: T_n=(1/log²2)·[ln2/(n(n-1)) - ln((n+1)/n)/(n-1) + ln((n+2)/(n+1))/n], asymptotic a_n~2log2/n², Σa_n=1. **At n_max=400: Σ_p a_p = 0.36187 vs measured |λ_0|^{χ_P}=0.35961, +0.6% rel error; Σ_n Λ(n)·a_n = 0.5206 vs measured |λ_0|^Λ=0.4968, +4.8% rel error.** For signed λ Rayleigh fails by factor 2 (left eigenvector ≠ const for signed weights). **Cramér closure**: vs B_crao 200 seeds at M=80, n=400: |λ_0| z=-1.79, |λ_1| z=-1.60, gap z=+2.10 — all within ±2σ Bonferroni (3-feature ≈ 2.39σ); F-B holds. vs B_supp z=+3.58 (uniform random over-spreads to high indices, false depression); vs B_par z=+2.02 (parity matched but lacks log-density profile). **A-grade hypothesis falsified**: |λ_0|/(π(N)/N) = 0.3596/0.195 = 1.844 — NOT a closed-form constant; the closed form IS Σ_p a_p, which is cost-equivalent to enumerating primes ≤ N. **Mechanism for closure mode E**: arithmetic-weighted PR leading resonance is a DENSITY-ONLY invariant at first moment — captured exactly by Σ_n h(n)·a_n where {a_n} is independent of h. Cramér model 1/log n + odd parity reproduces this expectation within sample noise. **Mayer-style dynamical-determinant representation of π(x) NOT opened**: there is no isolated arithmetic resonance distinct from the density-Rayleigh prediction. **Connections**: STRUCTURALLY DISTINCT from E2.13 Gowers (S85 detected HL → W-trick erases), E2.14 Anderson Lyapunov (S88 detected HL → W-trick erases), E2.16 anti-DPP (S95), E2.17 PH (S96), E2.19 subword (S104), E2.20 Mahler (S134), E2.21 Newman (S138) — all DETECT HL deviations; E2.22 (this work) shows the dynamical-spectral leading resonance is a 1-summing density integral that the Cramér model captures by construction. STRUCTURALLY DISTINCT from CLOSED line 320, 425